//! # Receive Key Ring — Offline Mailbox First-Message Trial Decryption
//!
//! A receive-side prekey ring (SPK + one-time keys) enabling offline-mailbox
//! first-message trial decryption, wired into the existing mesh decrypt-fail path.
//!
//! ## Design
//!
//! - SPK (Static Prekey): long-lived per-peer prekey, rotated every 1h on the
//!   mesh 1h tick alongside CRL GC
//! - OTK (One-Time Key): short-lived per-message key, pool of 8..24 keys,
//!   consumed on open (per-message forward secrecy), tracked by issuedTo
//! - Trial decrypt: iterate secrets (newest OTKs first, then SPKs, cap 28);
//!   on OTK hit, consume it; on SPK hit, establish session then hand off
//!   to double-ratchet for subsequent messages
//! - CRL gate: `is_revoked(sender)` as first check before ANY trial;
//!   also check epoch freshness consistent with P0 fail-closed
//! - Unknown-key requeue: messages that fail trial go to a bounded pending
//!   queue keyed by (sender, content-hash) with 6h TTL, retried when new
//!   prekeys arrive or peer reconnects; bounded size (suggest 1000)
//! - Encrypt-at-rest: keyring blobs are AEAD-encrypted under a storage key
//!   derived from the node master_seed via HKDF; never plaintext at rest
//! - Zeroize-on-drop for all key material
//!
//! ## Security invariants
//!
//! - CRL/epoch fail-closed (P0 just landed): stale epoch → reject, do not
//!   raise high-water on stale
//! - OTK per-message forward secrecy: consumed on successful open, never
//!   shared across peers
//! - No plaintext secrets at rest: AEAD-encrypted under storage key derived
//!   from master_seed via HKDF
//! - Zeroize-on-drop: all key material zeroized on drop
//!
//! ## Constants
//!
//! - `RECEIVE_KEY_ROTATION_MS`: 1 hour — SPK rotation interval, checked on the
//!   existing 1h tick (not every call)
//! - `RETENTION`: 6 hours — maximum age for a prekey to remain in the ring
//!   before GC evacuation
//! - `REPLENISH_FLOOR`: 8 — minimum unissued OTKs to maintain in the pool
//! - `REPLENISH_CEILING`: 24 — maximum total OTKs allowed in the pool
//! - `OPEN_SECRET_CAP`: 28 — maximum secrets iterated during trial decryption
//!
//! ## Security properties
//!
//! - CRL/epoch fail-closed: stale epoch → reject, do not raise high-water on stale
//! - OTK per-message forward secrecy: consumed on successful open, never shared
//!   across peers (track issuedTo)
//! - No plaintext secrets at rest: AEAD-encrypted under storage key derived from
//!   master_seed via HKDF; never plaintext at rest
//! - Zeroize-on-drop: all key material zeroized on drop
//!
//! ## Mailbox integration
//!
//! Trial-decrypt failures for unknown senders are requeued into a bounded pending
//! queue keyed by `(sender, content_hash)` with a 6h TTL. When new prekeys arrive
//! or the peer reconnects, the message is retried. Bounded size (suggest 1000) prevents
//! DoS. Messages that succeed in trial are delivered normally; SPK establishment
//! hands off to the double-ratchet for subsequent message protection.

use crate::core::crl::CrlStore;
use crate::core::encryption::{EncryptionManager, GhostKeyPair, KeyType};
use crate::core::persistence_manager::PersistenceManager;
use crate::core::mailbox::MailboxStore;
use dashmap::DashMap;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};
use std::time::Duration;
use tracing::{debug, info, warn};
